title: "The Six Stages of AI Adoption: a model built around identity, not tooling"
message: "If you use this model, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Osondu
    given-names: Victor
    affiliation: AI Tutorium
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-24"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://github.com/VictorOsondu/ai-adoption-model"
repository: "https://aitutorium.com"
abstract: >-
  A model for AI adoption that sorts people by internal experience rather than
  by tools deployed. Six stages — Nomad, Observer, Dabbler, Integrator,
  Architect, Innovator — each defined by a characteristic feeling and the
  question underneath it. The model's central claim is that the largest barrier
  to adoption is not a skill gap but a self-permission gap, most visible in the
  transition from Integrator to Architect.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI adoption
  - change management
  - professional development
  - identity
